Yamakan elections and obligations
---------------------------------
* FreeType is dual-licensed (FTL OR GPL-2.0-or-later). Yamakan elects
  GPL-2.0-or-later for FreeType (FTL credit clause is treated as
  GPL-incompatible for this combined work).
* fribidi remains under LGPL-2.1-or-later inside the WebAssembly module
  and stays replaceable as a separate module (notice retained; source
  offer / replaceability satisfied by shipping the unmodified npm
  package and this notice).
* The JASSUB JavaScript wrapper itself is MIT (see notices/jassub-LICENSE).
* Bundled native stack components (libass, fribidi, FreeType, HarfBuzz,
  Expat, Brotli, and related notices) travel with the wasm build under
  the SPDX expression above. No Yamakan copy of those sources is made;
  runtime is the unmodified npm dependency under node_modules/jassub.

Modifications
-------------
None. Consumed unmodified from npm with lockfile integrity.

Use in Yamakan
--------------
Live title preview (W12 / M15) behind JASSUB_ENABLED. Construction uses
queryFonts:false, pinned OFL fonts only (IBM Plex Sans Arabic), and
non-zero libassMemoryLimit / libassGlyphLimit. Worker and wasm are
served locally. Production CSP does not add 'wasm-unsafe-eval' until a
separate security-reviewed commit. Non-threaded wasm is preferred
(avoids COOP/COEP).
